diff --git a/core/types.odin b/core/types.odin
index 1789338..7e3e8d8 100644
--- a/core/types.odin
+++ b/core/types.odin
@@ -261,6 +261,76 @@ Crisis_State :: struct {
 	cooldowns:   [dynamic]Cooldown_Entry, // 4.2 — recently-resolved root causes (the re-fire gate, arch §6.4); engine memory, never serialized
 }
 
+// Window_Tick — one class's per-tick deltas inside the health rolling window
+// (4.3). The ring is FLAT: slot = class × window_ticks + (tick % window_ticks),
+// sized classes × window (health_ensure grows it deterministically). DELTAS
+// only — the layer DIFFS the flow's cumulative SLA accumulators each tick, so
+// a same-tick re-step sees delta 0 (re-step-safe; the 4.2 accepted-convention
+// note: the ring slot may be overwritten with zeros on a same-tick re-step —
+// the harness drains per step and the app never re-steps; replay never
+// re-steps, so replay equality holds).
+Window_Tick :: struct {
+	delivered:  u32,
+	dropped:    u32,
+	latency_ms: u64,
+}
+
+// Grace_Cell — one class's grace bookkeeping (4.3, E30). grace_left is the
+// countdown (0 = no grace: either never breached or SPENT — a spent grace
+// means the next breach drains immediately); healthy_streak is the sustained-
+// recovery gate before the gradual refill starts (the never-lose exploit
+// guard: consecutive episodes burn the shared countdown — a flapping line
+// never re-arms a full grace forever). Both are DERIVED (rebuilt identically
+// on replay from the serialized flow + tick history — same status as
+// sla_breach); the serializer emits only the non-zero grace_left rows
+// (absent-when-empty) so the T1 pins the countdown state.
+Grace_Cell :: struct {
+	grace_left:     u32,
+	healthy_streak: u32,
+}
+
+// Health_State — S5 Network Health (4.3, arch §6.5): the aggregate loss
+// condition. The meter drains on SUSTAINED per-class SLA breach (after the
+// class's grace countdown), recharges when every class is healthy, and
+// emptying it → Run_Lost (Error 404 — the terminal barrier freezes the run,
+// E17). The layer is gated by Run_State.health_enabled (run setup — a
+// disabled meter is INERT: no events, no drain, no Run_Lost; back-compat for
+// every pre-4.3 demo).
+//
+// Windowed measurement (the E30 seam the 3.4 comment deferred): the breach
+// latches are WINDOWED (rolling window_ticks of per-tick deltas), NOT the
+// 3.4 cumulative ones — the cumulative loss latch is monotone by contract, so
+// feeding the meter from it would drain forever after the first breach. The
+// window rings + sums + breach latches + grace cells + prev-diff scratch are
+// all DERIVED (never serialized — replay rebuilds them identically from the
+// serialized flow + events); only meter_pct + the non-zero grace rows + the
+// surge-win accumulators ride the T1 hash.
+Health_State :: struct {
+	meter_pct: u32, // 0..100; 0 = empty → Run_Lost (E17)
+	// per-class parallel arrays (indexed by class id, grown by health_ensure
+	// on the class's first demand — mirrors sla_ensure):
+	breach:          [dynamic]bool,       // WINDOWED breach latch (E30 enter/exit)
+	grace:           [dynamic]Grace_Cell, // per-class grace bookkeeping
+	prev_delivered:  [dynamic]u64,        // accumulator-diff scratch (last tick's totals)
+	prev_dropped:    [dynamic]u64,
+	prev_latency:    [dynamic]u64,
